# Video files never go in git. A single block of 1080p phone footage is
# 20-50 MB and git stores every version of it forever -- a handful of
# re-shoots would permanently bloat the repo for every future clone.
# Keep the recipe (blocks.json, kd-cut.py) in version control; keep the
# media on disk and backed up wherever you already back things up.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.MOV
*.MP4
*.wav
*.srt
raw/
out/
footage/*.mp4

# The README files ARE tracked -- they're the instructions, not the media.
!footage/README.txt
